/*
  core/masks/outcome_careless_skipcheck.spthy -- OPT-IN outcome row: the CARELESS user SKIPS the
  security check (an extension of the outcome matrix, like outcome_habituated_clickthrough).

  The default matrix gives Careless no 'compare' row: a careless user's verification stalls
  (safe-fail timeout). This row states the cited alternative: users under attentional degradation
  do not stall the ceremony -- they SKIP the fingerprint verification and proceed as if it passed
  (Whitten & Tygar 1999: users omit/mishandle the key-verification step; the check is what gets
  dropped, not the task). Skipping the comparison = accepting whatever was offered:

    Careless + compare -> credulous   (accepts ANY offered artifact -> a Mistake, like Naive)

  Opt-in, NOT global: P3 proves `mistake_requires_abstraction` under the default calibration
  (sigma2 -> Careless must not create compare mistakes there). A profile that includes THIS row
  models the skip-the-check hypothesis (secure_email v2 trio S1: concurrency-distracted sender
  skips the fingerprint check -> accepts the DY-substituted key). Persistent + read-only, seeded
  unconditionally -> closed theory; OnceCarelessSkipcheck bounds the seed.
*/

rule Seed_careless_skipcheck [color=#9b51e0]:
    [ ]
  --[ SeedCarelessSkipcheck() ]->
    [ !OutcomePolicy('Careless', 'compare', 'credulous') ]

restriction OnceCarelessSkipcheck:
  "All #i #j. SeedCarelessSkipcheck()@i & SeedCarelessSkipcheck()@j ==> #i = #j"
